        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>BAY</strong> denotes the estuary of the Dead Sea at the mouth of the Jordan (Joshua 15:5; 18:19), also the southern extremity of the same sea (15:2). The same Hebrew word is rendered “tongue” in Isaiah 11:15, where it is used with reference to the forked mouths of the Nile. Bay in Zechariah 6:3, 7 denotes the colour of horses, but the original Hebrew means strong, and is here used rather to describe the horses as fleet or spirited.",
