        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>KERIOTH</strong> cities. (1.) A town in the south of Judah (Joshua 15:25). Judas the traitor was probably a native of this place, and hence his name Iscariot. It has been identified with the ruins of el-Kureitein, about 10 miles south of Hebron. (See HAZOR [4]). (2.) A city of Moab (Jeremiah 48:24, 41), called Kirioth (Amos 2:2).",
