        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>KIRJATH-SANNAH</strong> city of the sannah; i.e., of the palm(?), Joshua 15:49; the same as Kirjath-sepher (15:16; Judges 1:11) and Debir (q.v.), a Canaanitish royal city included in Judah (Joshua 10:38; 15:49), and probably the chief seat of learning among the Hittites. It was about 12 miles to the south-west of Hebron.",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
