        "Note",
        "Note",
        """<strong>The Torah-meditation theme.</strong> Joshua opens with the same theme that opens the Psalter (Ps 1:2). The verb <em>hagah</em> ("meditate") originally means to mutter or murmur — meditation in the Hebrew Bible is verbal, the lips moving. Joshua’s leadership is grounded not in his sword-arm but in his constant rumination on Torah. The chapter sets the model for the ideal Davidic king of Deut 17:18–20.""",
