        "m",
        "",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        """<strong>Rahab’s confession.</strong> A Canaanite prostitute makes the most theologically explicit confession in the entire conquest narrative. Hebrews 11:31 and James 2:25 both highlight her as a paradigm of faith. Matthew 1:5 includes her in Jesus’s genealogy — one of four named women in the line. The book of Joshua’s ostensible policy of <em>ḥerem</em> is repeatedly complicated by the texts surrounding it: Rahab spared, the Gibeonites preserved, exclusions and inclusions cutting across ethnic lines.""",
