        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        """<strong>The mysterious commander.</strong> Joshua meets a figure with a drawn sword who refuses both the "for us" and "for our enemies" labels — "No, but I have come now as commander of Yahweh’s army." The episode parallels Moses at the burning bush ("take your sandals off"). Christian tradition has read the figure as a christophany; Jewish tradition as the angel of presence (cf. Exod 23:20–21). The encounter reframes the conquest: God is not a partisan; God’s side is its own.""",
