        "Note",
        """<strong>The sun and moon at Gibeon.</strong> Cited from "the book of Jashar" (also referenced in 2 Sam 1:18) — a lost early collection of Israelite war-poetry. Whether read literally or as poetic hyperbole, the line memorialized a battle so decisive that nature itself seemed to participate. Habakkuk 3:11 echoes the imagery. Of the Bible’s many lost books — Jashar, the Wars of the LORD (Num 21:14) — only fragments survive in citation.""",
